      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which identifiers count as tested? \"Anywhere in a requirement\" over-approximates. `cond-expand` stops at the first clause that holds, and `and` and `or` short-circuit, so in `(cond-expand (r7rs ...) (linux ...))` the expansion never looks at `linux`. Recording it would still make the artifact platform-specific.\n\nRecording only the identifiers the evaluation actually looked at, each with its value, is still sound, because nothing else decided the expansion. It also keeps such libraries portable. Suggest: \"each platform identifier that evaluating a requirement looked at\".",
