      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T13:49:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Refusing makes sense for a distributed artifact with no source (ADR 0012). But ADR 0001\u0027s sections are also the run-time cache, which records the source hash.\n\nFor a cached artifact whose source is available, a platform mismatch usually means a shared or copied cache, not \"built for somewhere else on purpose\". Recompiling, as for a stale artifact, is the useful response there. Refusing fails a program that would compile fine.\n\nSuggest: refuse when there\u0027s no source to rebuild from, and treat the mismatch as staleness when there is. That also gives the open question about multi-platform caches (line 65 onward) a default.",
