      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T13:49:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These procedures are a channel for platform information too, if a transformer calls them at expansion time. As written, the hook in item 3 is on `(features)`, so a transformer that calls `(platform-os)` would decide on the platform untracked: item 8\u0027s run-time alternative would become an untracked expansion-time route.\n\nStating the rule as \"every procedure whose result depends on a platform identifier reports through the hook\" covers these. It also covers anything later that exposes the byte order, such as native-endian bytevector accessors.",
